{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And all</b> — This indicates that Nebuchadnezzar was knowledgeable in the sciences, and he found each of these four to know ten measures more than every magician and conjurer. And it is possible that עשר is a plural form, like מעשרה שליטים (\"from ten rulers\"), because ten is a round number, and the author of Sefer Yetzirah said עשר ספירות בלי מה (\"ten sefirot of nothingness\"). And the חרטמים are not the אשפים, for it is written לקרוא לחרטומים ולאשפים (\"to call the magicians and the conjurers\"), and there I will explain them."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Hebrew text and verse numbering match standard editions of Ibn Ezra's commentary on Daniel; 'there I will explain them' apparently refers to his commentary on a later verse in Daniel where both terms recur."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:00.416759268Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}